<Defs>

<!--==========STRUCTURES MENTIONED IN SETTLEMENT GENERATION==========

-Citadels: Large structures that equate to massive castles. Home to multiple of the most prestigous bloodlines.
-Conservories: Giant structures used for housing multiple plants of multiple genomes. May also house or develop experimental genomes.
-Sanctuary: Giant cities that houseterratech citizens of all bloodlines and paths. Some even allow the Aquatic, though this is officially not documented.
-Spires: Massive structures that serves as a connection and collaboration between grounded terratech tribes and those of the sky. These spires are often extremely diverse and customized depending on which tribe has built them.
-Cathedral: Massive temples of unifications meant to prevent tribes from straying too far from getting too far tinro technology, like how the aquatic did.
-University: Massive locations where the young and newly welcomed are taught Terratech history. however, new developments are not created.
-Floronexus: Part of a massive tree that connects across the world, once connecting all organic tribes together. It has since hardened it's bark, and can no longer be interfaced with.
-Arboretum: A massive grove that contains many tree species, including experimental and alien ones.
-Chronovault: A massive dangerous vault that even terratech tribes avoid. Hold backups of many terratechnologies, but each are sealed away in 'time crystals'. Trying to interact or enter these crystals essentially takes you out of time, Permanently freezing you in place forever.
-Mausoleum: A large location where those of bloodlines or tribes are buried. Sometimes these have small settlements living nearby.
-Amberseals: A method of containment utilized by organic terratech, which can be tuned to an extreme degree. These amberseals are often used to contain prisoners, with the amber providing enough nutrients to keep them alive.
-Exagrove: A location of a tree that has grown to an incredible size, likely above the size of any other on the planet. Therefore it is very well protected, as what it can provide is highly valuable - and thus, may be exploited by others.

-->

</Defs>
